# bc_admits_blocked.ledger — ADMITTED PROGRAMS THAT NO COMPILER FIX CLOSES.
#
# THE SPLIT, AND WHY IT IS NOT A SKIP LIST. `bc_admits.ledger` is the queue: a
# row there is a borrow-check DEFECT with a root, and the intended way for that
# file to change is to SHRINK. This file holds the rows that are not defects and
# never were — a round that prices them is buying nothing, and four rounds in a
# row spent their pricing phase rediscovering that. Three kinds, and nothing
# else may be filed here:
#
#   LEGAL-AS-PORTED   the PORT is legal Rust as written, whatever upstream did.
#                     A fix that closed it would refuse a correct program. The
#                     owner's move is to re-port it (restore the turbofish, the
#                     non-Copy field, the closure, the parameterless `loop{}`)
#                     or to retire it — NOT to change the checker.
#   DIVERGENCE-*      Logos deliberately admits the shape, canonised in
#                     docs/DIVERGENCES.md or named by a `docs/spec/` clause.
#   OWNER-CORPUS      closing it would red LEGAL fixtures or the stdlib. The
#                     wall is named in the row, and the wall is what must be
#                     re-measured — not the row.
#
# ⚠ THE COVERAGE IS UNCHANGED. These programs did NOT move off the admit shelf.
# Each still has its own registered test `logos_00_bc_admit_<dir>_<name>` from
# the CMake glob, and each still asserts that the compile is SILENT. If one of
# them ever starts being refused that is still RED and still news — being a
# non-defect is not permission to change behaviour quietly.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS RE-VERIFIED, NOT CARRIED. A DECLINE IS A MEASUREMENT WITH A
# TIMESTAMP AND A WALL DECAYS. This file exists because a "five owner fixtures
# wall this block" verdict was carried for six rounds after four of the five had
# been REPAIRED, and re-pricing came back 5 -> 1. So every row carries the DATE
# its reason was last checked against the tree, and a row whose reason cannot be
# re-checked TODAY goes back to `bc_admits.ledger`, where the queue can see it.
# Re-verifying a row means opening the PORT and the WALL, not reading this file.
#
# Format:  <fixture> <root-id> <path relative to the repo root, no .logos>
#          # <REASON-TAG> <date verified> — <the evidence, in one line>
# The row itself is the same three columns `bc_admits.ledger` uses and is parsed
# by the same loop in `bc_admits_ledger_gate.sh`; the reason is a comment, so
# there is one row format in this tree and not two.
#
# Held by `logos_00_bc_admits_ledger` exactly as the queue is: every row has a
# file, every file under tests/imported/admit/ has a row in ONE of the two
# files, and EACH file's own `# TOTAL` is held against its own row count.
#
# ── 2026-09-04, the split: 124 -> 99 queue rows + 25 here ───────────────────
# EVERY ROW BELOW WAS RE-VERIFIED ON 2026-09-04 BY OPENING THE PORT, AND EVERY
# "walled by X" CLAIM BY OPENING X. What the re-verification CONTRADICTED, so
# that the next reader does not re-inherit it:
#   · E0713 x3 (enum-drop-access, issue-52059-…, issue-53773) are recorded
#     "retired, spec, by analogy with E0509". THE ANALOGY IS REFUTED AND THEY
#     ARE NOT HERE. `intrinsic.drop.skip-moved-out-paths` says drop SUPPRESSES a
#     moved-out sub-value; it says nothing about a `&mut` handed out PAST a
#     destructor that then writes through it, which is what these three do
#     (`drop_enum(d)` returns `opt.r` and `DropOpt::drop` stores 9 through it).
#     They stay in the queue as the aliasing holes they are.
#   · `do-not-ignore-lifetime-bounds-in-copy-proj--b` is recorded as a third A16
#     row. It is NOT on the admit shelf at all any more — it is a fail fixture,
#     tests/imported/fail/nll/, with a pinned diagnostic. The A16 group is TWO.
#   · the six `lifereg.R18` M-SIG rows are recorded "rejected twice" and are NOT
#     here. That decline decayed: every PROBES census through 09-07 prints
#     "lifereg.R18 8" and the root is SIX rows today, and M-SIG §6.1 (`Self`
#     substituted at the conformance site) LANDED in round 2026-09-04y after the
#     rejection. A partially-landed compiler direction is a queue row.

# ── 2026-09-07, STAGE 3 OF THE RE-PORT: 25 -> 12 ────────────────────────────
# EVERY ONE OF THE 25 ROWS WAS RE-PORTED AS-IS FROM ITS UPSTREAM TEST at the
# commit its port cites (scripts/report-worksheet.py, rustc checkout at
# 4b0c9d76a). THIRTEEN ROWS LEFT THIS FILE, and the split of the thirteen is the
# finding: EIGHT of them were not blocked at all — the PORT had moved the
# construct to where the rule flips, and restoring the construct makes them
# ordinary admitted DEFECTS, now rows in bc_admits.ledger. FIVE re-ported to a
# REFUSAL at the same construct and are fail fixtures with the sentence pinned.
# ⚠ NO COMPILER SOURCE WAS TOUCHED IN THAT ROUND. `git diff --stat` over src/
# and include/ is empty; every verdict below is the unmodified compiler's.
# What each surviving row now carries: the BUCKET it landed in, and the file
# itself carries the full audit trail (`// Original path:`, the upstream
# construct with its line numbers, and `// Modifications:`).
#   BUCKET 3, blessed divergence (7) — the construct cannot exist here, and the
#     clause is cited BY ID in the port. Five E0509 rows against
#     `intrinsic.drop.skip-moved-out-paths` (docs/spec/expressions.md), and the
#     clause was RE-VERIFIED BY RUNNING IT: a two-Drop struct with `let g = s.f`
#     prints INNER_DROPS=1 S_DROPS=1 — no leak, no double free. Two A16 rows
#     against DIVERGENCES.md A16 (structural auto-Copy, canonised 2026-08-24).
#   BUCKET 4, implementation hole (3) — the re-port needs something the language
#     does not have. Both `multiple-sources-*` rows need an explicit LIFETIME
#     argument in a turbofish (`f::<'_>(..)` -> "unexpected type node code 131",
#     while `call::<i64>()` compiles); `issue-64173-unused-lifetimes` needs a
#     const-expression array length. Both are entries in unrowed_backlog.ledger.
#   OWNER-CORPUS (2) — the two `regions-*-anon` ports are FAITHFUL as they stand
#     (an elided `&` in a declaration, verbatim) and their wall was re-measured
#     by direct listing: 195 bare-`&` declaration sites in 124 files (was
#     recorded as 134 in 101 — it GREW), plus the explicit pass pin
#     `bc_enumpldlt_placeholder_payload_lifetime`. ⚠ NOT a blessed divergence:
#     no clause canonises it, searched 2026-09-07.
# ⚠ WHERE THE E0392 WALL STANDS, RE-MEASURED 2026-09-07 rather than carried:
#   6559 pass fixtures scanned for a struct/enum declaring a lifetime parameter
#   its body never mentions — FIVE, in five files. The recorded "five pass
#   fixtures" has NOT decayed.

